- **N34 — medium, blocker:** [review_bundle.go:3499](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4018275949/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:3499) skips adopted exemptions when review bundles are disabled. An exempt aggregate can close successfully yet remain unapproved in `review verify`.
- **N35 — low, follow-up:** [roadmaps.go:398](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4018275949/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/roadmaps.go:398) suppresses predecessor warnings based on review approval or exemption, without requiring closure.
- **N36 — medium, blocker:** [review_bundle.go:3535](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4018275949/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:3535) marks failed exemptions as inherited. The roadmap child collector skips them, allowing the roadmap’s own review verification to remain approved over a rejected descendant. R8-N32 remains partial.

Focused policy tests, existing child-standing regressions, `go vet`, artifact-check and surface-check passed. Artifact-check reported 923 warnings; surface-check reported zero findings. The worktree remains unchanged.

Applied the review workflow and backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules. No attestation was recorded.

